# whoever has the namespace object of a module reads its exports by name, which names no variable: an operation that names the module and gives a value lets the exports escape
# library.js: export function five() { return 5 } export function six() { return 6 }
# main.js: import "./library.js"; import("./library.js").then(ns => print(ns.five())); print(Object.create(namespace of library.js).six())
# The module is imported by a statement too, so it is no module that the host alone asks for, and no flag of its record says that anybody holds its namespace object
